    INSERT INTO staged_systems (manufacturer_id, source_document_id, name, product_code, category, subcategory, description, notes, custom_technical_attributes)
    VALUES (v_mfr, v_doc, 'Steel Deck Subframe', 'DWA-SSF', 'Subfloor', 'Steel subframe', 'Generic RFQ template for a steel deck subframe: bearers, joists, posts, base plates, connections, coatings and isolation items. Generic RFQ template, not a manufacturer-certified system or engineering specification. Final sizes, grades, spacings, footings and compliance must be confirmed by the builder/engineer before ordering.', 'Code DWA-SSF. VARIABLES TO CONFIRM: Engineer''s design and spans; steel section and thickness; coating system and corrosivity category; connection and anchor design; footing type; board fixing system; on-site welding/cutting (fire risk, coating repair); BAL; strata/balcony rules. OPEN QUESTIONS: [?] Hollow sections galvanised after fabrication need vent/drain holes [R] — who details this? [?] Which steel supplier/fabricator will quote? [?] Typical coating Perth builders specify for exposed decks? Standards referenced (paywalled — read at source, not reproduced): NCC 2022 Housing Provisions 2.2 and 3.4; AS 1684; AS/NZS 1604.1 (H3 above ground; H4/H5 ground contact); AS 3660.1 termite management; AS 3959 bushfire (BAL); AS/NZS 1170.1 imposed actions; AS 4312 atmospheric corrosivity (C1–C5, CX). Bushfire (BAL) overlay — AS 3959:2018 sets what the subfloor can be made from (secondary sources; confirm in the standard) [S]. BAL-12.5/19: unenclosed subfloor with members under 400 mm above ground needs bushfire-resisting timber or non-combustible members, or shielding/enclosure. BAL-29: unenclosed subfloor must meet BAL-29 clauses; verandah posts must be non-combustible or hardwood. BAL-40: post/column/stump clause not retrieved. Bushfire-resisting timbers are 750 kg/m3 or denser (Table E1). Add a BAL question to the order. STATUS: placeholder lists for builder + engineer review; not advice.', '[{"label": "Template type", "value": "Generic RFQ template \u2014 not manufacturer-certified"}, {"label": "Frame material", "value": "Steel \u2014 section, thickness and coating per engineer"}, {"label": "Structural grade", "value": "As specified by engineering"}, {"label": "Non-combustible", "value": "Steel members are non-combustible \u2014 confirm for the BAL context"}]'::jsonb)
