    VALUES (v_mfr, v_doc, 'Aluminium Deck Subframe', 'DWA-ASF', 'Subfloor', 'Aluminium subframe', 'Generic RFQ template for an aluminium deck subframe: joists, bearers, posts or pedestals, connectors and isolation items. Spans, sizes, fixings and compliance must come from the manufacturer''s data and the engineer. Branded cards should replace this starter as manufacturers are onboarded.', 'Code DWA-ASF. VARIABLES TO CONFIRM: Manufacturer span tables; maximum joist spacing for the chosen boards; load; corrosivity category and finish; galvanic isolation details [S]; fixings grade (316 stainless coastal [S]). OPEN QUESTIONS: [?] Which aluminium standard applies (AS/NZS 1664?) and who signs off spans? [?] Which brands are available in WA? Standards referenced (paywalled — read at source, not reproduced): NCC 2022 Housing Provisions 2.2 and 3.4; AS 1684; AS/NZS 1604.1 (H3 above ground; H4/H5 ground contact); AS 3660.1 termite management; AS 3959 bushfire (BAL); AS/NZS 1170.1 imposed actions; AS 4312 atmospheric corrosivity (C1–C5, CX). Bushfire (BAL) overlay — AS 3959:2018 sets what the subfloor can be made from (secondary sources; confirm in the standard) [S]. BAL-12.5/19: unenclosed subfloor with members under 400 mm above ground needs bushfire-resisting timber or non-combustible members, or shielding/enclosure. BAL-29: unenclosed subfloor must meet BAL-29 clauses; verandah posts must be non-combustible or hardwood. BAL-40: post/column/stump clause not retrieved. Bushfire-resisting timbers are 750 kg/m3 or denser (Table E1). Add a BAL question to the order. STATUS: placeholder lists for builder + engineer review; not advice.', '[{"label": "Template type", "value": "Generic starter \u2014 usually a branded system with its own span tables"}, {"label": "Frame material", "value": "Aluminium \u2014 profile and finish are manufacturer-specific"}]'::jsonb)
