    VALUES (v_mfr, v_doc, 'Coastal Timber Deck Subframe', 'DWA-TSF-C', 'Subfloor', 'Timber subframe (coastal)', 'Generic RFQ template for a timber deck subframe near the coast, with corrosion-resistant fixings and post bases. Corrosivity category, treatment, coatings and fixings must be confirmed by the builder/engineer against the site''s AS 4312 category before ordering. Generic RFQ template, not a manufacturer-certified system or engineering specification. Final sizes, grades, spacings, footings and compliance must be confirmed by the builder/engineer before ordering.', 'Code DWA-TSF-C. VARIABLES TO CONFIRM: AS 4312 category for the exact lot; distance/exposure (surf beach vs sheltered); shade and spray exposure; stainless grade availability; concrete exposure class; maintenance plan. OPEN QUESTIONS: [?] What do WA builders use within the first 1–2 km of the coast? [?] Who stocks 316 stainless post bases, brackets and bolts in WA and at what price? Standards referenced (paywalled — read at source, not reproduced): NCC 2022 Housing Provisions 2.2 and 3.4; AS 1684; AS/NZS 1604.1 (H3 above ground; H4/H5 ground contact); AS 3660.1 termite management; AS 3959 bushfire (BAL); AS/NZS 1170.1 imposed actions; AS 4312 atmospheric corrosivity (C1–C5, CX). Bushfire (BAL) overlay — AS 3959:2018 sets what the subfloor can be made from (secondary sources; confirm in the standard) [S]. BAL-12.5/19: unenclosed subfloor with members under 400 mm above ground needs bushfire-resisting timber or non-combustible members, or shielding/enclosure. BAL-29: unenclosed subfloor must meet BAL-29 clauses; verandah posts must be non-combustible or hardwood. BAL-40: post/column/stump clause not retrieved. Bushfire-resisting timbers are 750 kg/m3 or denser (Table E1). Add a BAL question to the order. STATUS: placeholder lists for builder + engineer review; not advice.', '[{"label": "Template type", "value": "Generic RFQ template \u2014 coastal variant of the timber subframe"}, {"label": "Corrosivity category", "value": "Confirm C3 / C4 / C5 / CX under AS 4312 for the exact lot \u2014 do not rely on a distance rule [S]"}, {"label": "Fixings", "value": "316 stainless; avoid electroplated [S]"}, {"label": "Frame material", "value": "H3 minimum above ground; consider H4 or Class 1 hardwood near ground or in salt spray [S]"}]'::jsonb)
    RETURNING id INTO v_sys;
